id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60ApZs","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-30T17:14:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-30T17:32:53Z","body":"> I don't know if we do this with other body types currently.\r\n\r\nWe do not. Both the Jolt and Godot Physics servers will wake `RigidBody3D` up when setting any transform.\r\n\r\nIt's easy enough to change I guess, but you shouldn't really be hammering `RigidBody3D` with ~~the same~~ any transform over and over in the first place, as that has been shown to cause all kinds of jank, so I'm not sure that's a use-case worth catering to. ~~I would imagine that holds true for `SoftBody3D` as well.~~\r\n\r\nEDIT: Oh right, there's not really a transform to compare against in the case of soft bodies anyway, since it's all just a lose collection of points, so nevermind I guess. On top of that we're forced to interpret the transform as relative. So I guess the best we could do is check if it's an identity matrix being set.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3020068460/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"lau